@inproceedings{DBLP:conf/icai/GriolPCM09,
  abstract  = {
               Context-aware systems in combination with mobile devices offer new opportunities in the areas
               of knowledge representati\'{o}n, natural language processing and intelligent information
               retrieval. They also bring new opportunities for end users by gathering context data and
               adapting the system behaviour taking into account this information. In this paper, we present a
               layered architecture for the design of context-aware systems where an intelligent speech-based
               engine is integrated to use spontaneous speech to access the different sendees. These services
               are personalized by taking into account context information included in specific user profiles.
               An application of our architecture to design a railway information system is also described and
               evaluated.
               },
